## Static decision table

| Existing source case | Corrected invariant result |
| --- | --- |
| Exact duplicate, parent-equal policy, empty actual symbols | Permitted by the changed-symbol guard; complete identity and evidence checks still apply. |
| Exact duplicate, parent-equal policy, nonempty actual symbols | Rejected by the changed-symbol guard. |
| Exact duplicate, different policy | No exemption; even if declared symbols match, the complete status/evidence guard rejects the different policy. |
| Changed-policy non-duplicate, exact declared symbols | Original behavior preserved. |
| Changed-policy non-duplicate, empty or mismatched symbols | Rejected. |
| Pre-validation invalid, including rendering rejection | Unchanged separate `_validate_invalid_identity` path. |
| Duplicate-only or mixed batch record construction | Both constructors retain actual validation, identity and evidence; the existing critic requirement remains exact for other testable candidates. |

This table is source reasoning only. No candidate, record, event or synthetic case was constructed or executed for it.

## Source trace

`StructuralTemplateV5` continues requiring a nonempty declared edit scope. The concrete validator derives actual symbols from before/after source bundles. Runtime requires empty actual symbols for a parent-identical revision, marks it `exact_duplicate`, and returns before quick screening; `QuickScreenCandidateV5` therefore keeps its declared-symbol equality guard unchanged.

Runtime `_expected_records` and the concrete production record factory each pass `candidate.validation` unchanged to `ExperimentRecordV5`; artifact decoding also invokes that common constructor. The corrected invariant therefore applies to both independent factories and decoding without any field, encoding, identity, payload union or schema change. `_verify_finalized_candidate_origin` still compares record validation exactly with the durable validation stage and checks the exact-duplicate semantic outcome. No fabricated critic or performance evidence is introduced.

